    {
      "id": "claim_480465ff53204d5baf8082e475ecb4b3",
      "statement": "A session token is \"<doName>:<secret>\"; the user DO stores only SHA-256(secret) keyed as the session record and authenticate() routes by idFromName of the token's first part. For password login the browser derives an argon2id hash with the public SERVICE_SALT + username and the server stores a further SHA-256 of it, so the server never sees the plaintext password and the expensive hash runs client-side.",
